    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet in the highly regarded area of Creaghduff, Coosan, Athlone, this superbly maintained four-bedroom, three-bathroom bungalow offers an excellent combination of generous accommodation, beautiful gardens and a highly desirable location on the popular Coosan Point Road.\n\nFrom the moment you arrive, it is clear that this is a home that has been lovingly cared for and maintained to a very high standard. The property is surrounded by a large, mature garden which is a particular highlight, enjoying an abundance of sunlight and an array of colour throughout the seasons. The generous outdoor space provides an ideal setting for family life, entertaining or simply enjoying the peace and privacy of the surrounding landscape.\n\nInternally, the property offers bright, spacious and comfortable accommodation. There are two generous living rooms, providing excellent flexibility for family living, relaxation and entertaining. These rooms connect beautifully with the warm and homely kitchen, creating a welcoming heart to the home.\n\nThe kitchen has a wonderful connection with the outdoors, opening directly onto the patio area. From here, the garden and surrounding landscape can be enjoyed to their fullest, creating a particularly attractive space for outdoor dining, entertaining or relaxing during the summer months.\n\nThe accommodation comprises four well-proportioned bedrooms and three bathrooms, providing ample space for a growing family, visiting guests or those looking for additional flexibility within the home.\n\nOutside, the property continues to impress. The extensive gardens offer plenty of space for children, gardening enthusiasts and outdoor entertaining, while the property also benefits from substantial additional storage in the form of a large steel-tech shed and a detached block-built shed. These buildings offer excellent versatility and could accommodate everything from garden equipment and storage to hobbies, workshop use or recreational equipment.\n\nThe property enjoys a highly sought-after position on Coosan Point Road, within easy reach of Athlone town and a wide range of local amenities.\n\nFor families, Coosan National School is conveniently located within the local area, providing an excellent primary school option close to home.\n\nEveryday shopping is also well catered for, with SuperValu on Ballymahon Road nearby, while Athlone town and its wider range of shops, cafés, restaurants and services are also easily accessible.\n\nFor commuters, the property benefits from excellent road connectivity, with the M6 motorway readily accessible via the Coosan/Athlone road network, providing convenient links towards Dublin, Galway and beyond. The M6 is accessed in the vicinity of Junctions 10 and 11.\n\nSporting and recreational amenities are also a major attraction of the area. Athlone GAA Club is nearby, along with a wide range of other sporting facilities and clubs, while the proximity to Coosan Point and Lough Ree provides further opportunities to enjoy the outdoors.\n\nCombining generous accommodation, beautifully maintained gardens, excellent storage and a superb location close to schools, shopping, sport and transport links, Creaghduff offers a wonderful opportunity to acquire a substantial family home in one of Athlone's most popular residential areas.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the space, condition, gardens and setting this property has to offer."
      },
